threshold\">[tax_threshold: $5 million]<\/span>, implemented in every country around the world.\n<br><br><span id=\"tax_country_name\">[tax_country_name: In the U.S.]<\/span>, the tax revenues collected would be <span id=\"tax_revenue\">[tax_revenue: $514 billion]<\/span> per year (that is, <span id=\"tax_revenue_gdp\">[tax_revenue_gdp: 2]<\/span>% of <span id=\"tax_country_gdp\">[tax_country_gdp: U.S. GDP]<\/span>), while it would be <span id=\"LIC_revenue\">[LIC_revenue: $1 billion]<\/span> in all low-income countries combined (700 million people live in a low-income country, most of them in Africa).\nEach country would retain part of the revenues it collects and use it for different domestic purposes. The remaining part would be pooled globally to finance sustainable development in low-income countries.\n<br><br><b>What percentage of the global wealth tax revenue should be allocated to each category?<\/b> <br><b>The total allocation must sum to 100%.<\/b><br><br>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function() {\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_conjoint\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tconst time_before = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"time_field\");\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"duration_conjoint\", Date.now()\/1000 - time_before);\n\t\n\n   jQuery(this.getQuestionContainer()).find(\".ChoiceStructure\").prepend(\"<div style='text-align:right;font-weight:bold;padding-bottom:10px;line-height:1.1'>\"+\n\n             \"<span class='totCheck' style='display:none;color:green'>&#10004; <\/span><span class='sum_name'>Total<\/span>\"+\n\n             \": <span class='totWrap'><span class='total'>0<\/span>%<\/span><\/span>\");\n\n       mfCsSliders(this);\n\t\n\t\/\/ Loads CSV and create variables from the column corresponding to Q_Language\n\t$j(document).ready(function($j){\t\n\t\t$j.ajax({\n\t\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\/\/ Iterate through the rows and create variables dynamically\n\t\t\tfor (let i = 1; i < rows.length-1; i++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst name = rows[i][0]; \/\/ Assuming the row name is in the first column\n\t\t\t\tconst value = rows[i][col];\n\t\t\t\twindow[name] = value; \n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\t$j(\".\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`Variable ${name} created with value: ${value}`);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t\t});\n\t});\n\n});","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"revenue_split_few","QuestionID":"QID1","QuestionType":"Slider","Selector":"HSLIDER","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","CSSliderMin":0,"CSSliderMax":100,"GridLines":20,"SnapToGrid":true,"NumDecimals":"0","ShowValue":true,"CustomStart":false,"NotApplicable":false,"MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Imagine a wealth tax applied to households with a net worth above [tax_threshold: $5 million], im...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Domestic: Education and Healthcare"},"2":{"Display":"Domestic: Social welfare programs"},"3":{"Display":"Domestic: Reduction in the federal income tax"},"4":{"Display":"Domestic: Reduction of the deficit"},"5":{"Display":"Global: Education, Healthcare and Renewable energy in low-income countries"}},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">variant_split<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 1 <\/span>","LeftOperand":"variant_split","LogicType":"EmbeddedField","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"1","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":false},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Randomization":{"Advanced":{"FixedOrder":["{~Randomized~}","{~Randomized~}","{~Randomized~}","{~Randomized~}","{~Randomized~}"],"RandomSubSet":[],"RandomizeAll":["1","2","3","4","5"],"ScaleReversal":[],"TotalRandSubset":0,"Undisplayed":[]},"ConsistentScaleReversal":false,"EvenPresentation":false,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"Advanced"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Imagine a wealth tax applying on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all countries around the world.\nIn the U.S., the tax revenues collected would be $430 billion per year (that ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Global: Education, Healthcare and Renewable energy in low-income countries<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> $e{100 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/1 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/2 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/3 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/4 } <\/span>","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"EqualTo","QuestionID":"QID1","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","RightOperand":"$e{100 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/1 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/2 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/3 - q:\/\/QID1\/ChoiceNumericEntryValue\/4 }","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Require total sum of 100","libraryID":null,"messageID":null,"subMessageID":"VE_IMPORTANCE_TOTAL"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Imaginez un imp\u00f4t sur la fortune s'appliquant aux m\u00e9nages avec un patrimoine sup\u00e9rieur \u00e0 <span id=\"tax_threshold\">5 millions de livres sterling<\/span>, mis en \u0153uvre dans tous les pays.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span id=\"tax_country_name\">Aux \u00c9tats-Unis<\/span>, les recettes collect\u00e9es s'\u00e9l\u00e8veraient \u00e0 <span id=\"tax_revenue\">430 milliards de dollars<\/span> par an (soit <span id=\"tax_revenue_gdp\">2<\/span>\u00a0% du <span id=\"tax_country_gdp\">[tax_country_gdp: U.S. GDP]<\/span>), alors qu'elles s'\u00e9l\u00e8veraient \u00e0 <span class=\"LIC_revenue\">1 milliard d'euros<\/span> dans l'ensemble des pays \u00e0 bas revenus (700 millions de personnes vivent dans un pays \u00e0 bas revenus, la plupart en Afrique). Chaque pays conserverait une partie des recettes qu\u2019il collecte et l\u2019utiliserait \u00e0 diff\u00e9rentes fins nationales. La partie restante serait mise en commun au niveau mondial pour financer le d\u00e9veloppement durable dans les pays \u00e0 bas revenus.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nQuel pourcentage des recettes de l\u2019imp\u00f4t mondial sur la fortune devrait \u00eatre allou\u00e9 \u00e0 chaque cat\u00e9gorie\u00a0? Le total doit faire 100\u00a0%.<br \/>\n\u00a0","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"National\u00a0:\u00a0\u00c9ducation et sant\u00e9"},"2":{"Display":"National\u00a0: Protection sociale (RSA, allocations familiales, cr\u00e8ches, minimum vieillesse, AAH...)"},"3":{"Display":"National : R\u00e9duction de l\u2019imp\u00f4t sur le revenu"},"4":{"Display":"National : R\u00e9duction du d\u00e9ficit"},"5":{"Display":"Mondial : \u00c9ducation, sant\u00e9 et \u00e9nergies renouvelables dans les pays \u00e0 bas revenus"}},"Labels":[]}},"NextChoiceId":13,"NextAnswerId":4,"Labels":[],"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Imagine a wealth tax applied to households with a net worth above <span id=\"tax_threshold\">[tax_threshold: $5 million]<\/span>, implemented in every country around the world.\n<br><br><span id=\"tax_country_name\">[tax_country_name: In the U.S.]<\/span>, the tax revenues collected would be <span id=\"tax_revenue\">[tax_revenue: $514 billion]<\/span> per year (that is, <span id=\"tax_revenue_gdp\">[tax_revenue_gdp: 2]<\/span>% of <span id=\"tax_country_gdp\">[tax_country_gdp: U.S. GDP]<\/span>), while it would be <span id=\"LIC_revenue\">[LIC_revenue: $1 billion]<\/span> in all low-income countries combined (700 million people live in a low-income country, most of them in Africa).\nEach country would retain part of the revenues it collects and use it for different domestic purposes. The remaining part would be pooled globally to finance sustainable development in low-income countries.\n<br><br><b>What percentage of the global wealth tax revenue should be allocated to each category?<\/b> <br><b>The total allocation must sum to 100%.<\/b><br><br>","Answers":{"1":{"Display":0},"2":{"Display":5},"3":{"Display":10},"4":{"Display":15},"5":{"Display":20},"6":{"Display":25},"7":{"Display":30},"8":{"Display":35},"9":{"Display":40},"10":{"Display":45},"11":{"Display":50},"12":{"Display":55},"13":{"Display":60},"14":{"Display":65},"15":{"Display":70},"16":{"Display":75},"17":{"Display":80},"18":{"Display":85},"19":{"Display":90},"20":{"Display":95},"21":{"Display":100}}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"Below are different ways to transfer resources to help reduce poverty in a low-income country.\u00a0 H..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Below are different ways to transfer resources to help reduce poverty in a low-income country.&nbsp;<br>How do you evaluate each of these options?<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"transfer_how","QuestionID":"QID10","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidth":25,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Below are different ways to transfer resources to help reduce poverty in a low-income country.\u00a0 H...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Cash transfers to parents (child allowances), to the disabled and to the elderly"},"2":{"Display":"Unconditional transfers to the national government"},"3":{"Display":"Transfers to the national government conditioned on the use of funds for poverty reduction programs"},"4":{"Display":"Unconditional transfers to local authorities (municipality, village chief...)"},"5":{"Display":"Transfers to local NGOs with democratic decision-making processes"},"6":{"Display":"Transfers to public development aid agencies which then finance suitable projects"},"7":{"Display":"Unconditional cash transfers to each household"}},"ChoiceOrder":["6",3,2,4,5,1,"7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Vous trouverez ci-dessous diff\u00e9rentes mani\u00e8res de transf\u00e9rer des ressources pour r\u00e9duire la pauvret\u00e9 dans un pays \u00e0 bas revenus.<br \/>\nComment jugez-vous chacune de ces options ?","Choices":{"6":{"Display":"Transferts vers des agences publiques d'aide au d\u00e9veloppement qui financent des projets appropri\u00e9s"},"3":{"Display":"Transferts au gouvernement national conditionn\u00e9s \u00e0 l&#39;utilisation des fonds pour des programmes de r\u00e9duction de la pauvret\u00e9"},"2":{"Display":"Transferts inconditionnels au gouvernement national"},"4":{"Display":"Transferts inconditionnels aux autorit\u00e9s locales (commune, chef de village...)"},"5":{"Display":"Transferts vers des ONG locales ayant des processus d\u00e9cisionnels d\u00e9mocratiques"},"1":{"Display":"Transferts mon\u00e9taires aux parents (allocations familiales), aux personnes handicap\u00e9es et aux personnes \u00e2g\u00e9es"},"7":{"Display":"Transferts mon\u00e9taires inconditionnels \u00e0 chaque m\u00e9nage"}},"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Un