hutzpartei"},"9":{"Display":"dieBasis"}},"QuestionText":"Even if you did not vote in the 2021 German federal election, please indicate the candidate that you were most likely to\r\nhave voted for or who represents your views more closely."},"ES-ES":{"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Biden"},"2":{"Display":"Triunfo"},"3":{"Display":"Jorgensen"},"4":{"Display":"Hawkins"},"5":{"Display":"Prefiero no decirlo"}},"QuestionText":"Incluso si no vot\u00f3 en las elecciones presidenciales de EE. UU. de 2020, indique el candidato\/a por el que es m\u00e1s probable que haya votado o que represente sus puntos de vista m\u00e1s de cerca."},"FR":{"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"CDU\/CSU"},"10":{"Display":"Die PARTEI"},"11":{"Display":"Sonstige"},"2":{"Display":"SPD"},"3":{"Display":"Grune"},"4":{"Display":"Freie W\u00e4hler"},"5":{"Display":"Ich m\u00f6chte das nicht beantworten"},"6":{"Display":"AfD"},"7":{"Display":"Die Linke"},"8":{"Display":"Tierschutzpartei"},"9":{"Display":"dieBasis"}},"QuestionText":"M\u00eame si vous n&#39;avez pas vot\u00e9 aux \u00e9lections f\u00e9d\u00e9rales allemandes de 2021, veuillez indiquer le candidat pour lequel vous \u00e9tiez le plus susceptible d&#39;avoir vot\u00e9 ou qui repr\u00e9sente le mieux vos opinions."}},"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":13,"QuestionDescription":"Even if you did not vote in the 2021 German federal election, please indicate the candidate that...","QuestionID":"QID48","QuestionText":"Even if you did not vote in the 2021 German federal election, please indicate the candidate that you were most likely to\nhave voted for or who represents your views more closely.","QuestionText_Unsafe":"Even if you did not vote in the 2021 German federal election, please indicate the candidate that you were most likely to\nhave voted for or who represents your views more closely.","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SACOL","SubSelector":"TX","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID49","SecondaryAttribute":"Do you support or oppose a tax on millionaires of all countries to finance low-income countries?...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Strongly oppose"},"2":{"Display":"Somewhat oppose"},"3":{"Display":"Neither support nor oppose"},"4":{"Display":"Somewhat support"},"5":{"Display":"Strongly support"}},"Configuration":{"LabelPosition":"BELOW","QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"DataExportTag":"global_tax_support","DataVisibility":{"Hidden":false,"Private":false},"DefaultChoices":false,"GradingData":[],"Language":{"DE":{"QuestionText":"Unterst\u00fctzen Sie eine Steuer auf Million\u00e4re aller L\u00e4nder, um L\u00e4nder mit niedrigem Einkommen zu finanzieren oder lehnen Sie\u00a0so eine Steuer ab?<br \/>\nDamit w\u00fcrden Infrastruktur und \u00f6ffentliche Dienstleistungen wie der Zugang zu Trinkwasser, Gesundheitsversorgung und Bildung finanziert.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Entschiedene Ablehnung"},"2":{"Display":"Etwas Ablehnung"},"3":{"Display":"Gleichg\u00fcltig oder wei\u00df nicht"},"4":{"Display":"Etwas Unterst\u00fctzung"},"5":{"Display":"Starke Unterst\u00fctzung"}}},"EN-GB":{"QuestionText":"Do you support or oppose a tax on millionaires of all countries to finance low-income countries?<br \/>\nSuch tax would finance infrastructure and public services such as access to drinking water, healthcare, and education.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Strongly oppose"},"2":{"Display":"Somewhat oppose"},"3":{"Display":"Indifferent or don't know"},"4":{"Display":"Somewhat support"},"5":{"Display":"Strongly support"}}},"ES-ES":{"QuestionText":"\u00bfEst\u00e1 a favor o en contra de un impuesto a los millonarios\/as de todos los pa\u00edses para financiar a los pa\u00edses de bajos ingresos?<br \/>\nEsto financiar\u00eda la infraestructura y los servicios p\u00fablicos, como el acceso al agua potable, la atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y la educaci\u00f3n.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Totalmente en contra"},"2":{"Display":"Levemente en contra"},"3":{"Display":"Indiferente o no sabe"},"4":{"Display":"Levemente a favor"},"5":{"Display":"Totalmente a favor"}}},"FR":{"QuestionText":"\u00cates-vous favorable ou oppos\u00e9\u22c5e \u00e0 une taxe sur tous les millionnaires du monde pour financer les pays \u00e0 faibles revenus ?<br \/>\n<br \/>\nCela financerait des infrastructures et des services publics tels que l'acc\u00e8s \u00e0 l'eau potable, la sant\u00e9 et l'\u00e9ducation.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Tr\u00e8s oppos\u00e9\u22c5e"},"2":{"Display":"Plut\u00f4t oppos\u00e9\u22c5e"},"3":{"Display":"Indiff\u00e9rent\u22c5e ou ne sais pas"},"4":{"Display":"Plut\u00f4t favorable"},"5":{"Display":"Tr\u00e8s favorable"}}}},"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":6,"QuestionDescription":"Do you support or oppose a tax on millionaires of all countries to finance low-income countries?...","QuestionID":"QID49","QuestionText":"Do you support or oppose a tax on millionaires of all countries to finance low-income countries?<br>\nThis would finance infrastructure and public services such as access to drinking water, healthcare, and education.","QuestionText_Unsafe":"Do you support or oppose a tax on millionaires of all countries to finance low-income countries?<br>\nThis would finance infrastructure and public services such as access to drinking water, healthcare, and education.","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID5","SecondaryAttribute":"Ci-dessous, nous d\u00e9crivons une mesure politique, sur laquelle nous allons sonder votre opinion. P..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div>Ci-dessous, nous d\u00e9crivons une mesure politique, sur laquelle nous allons sonder votre opinion.<br><\/div>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Plan mondial pour le climat :<\/strong><\/u><br>\n<br>\nEn 2015, tous les pays se sont mis d'accord pour contenir le r\u00e9chauffement climatique \"bien en-dessous de +2 \u00b0C\". Pour limiter le r\u00e9chauffement climatique \u00e0 ce niveau, <strong>il existe une quantit\u00e9 maximale de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre que nous pouvons \u00e9mettre \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle mondiale<\/strong>.<br>\n<br>\nPour respecter cet objectif climatique, un nombre limit\u00e9 de permis d'\u00e9mission de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre pourrait \u00eatre cr\u00e9\u00e9 \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle mondiale. Les entreprises polluantes devraient acheter des permis pour couvrir leurs \u00e9missions. Une telle politique <strong>obligerait les<\/strong> <strong>compagnies p\u00e9troli\u00e8res \u00e0 payer<\/strong>&nbsp;pour leurs \u00e9missions et augmenterait progressivement le prix des combustibles fossiles. <strong>Des prix plus \u00e9lev\u00e9s encourageraient les m\u00e9nages et les entreprises \u00e0 utiliser moins de combustibles fossiles, r\u00e9duisant ainsi les \u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre.<\/strong><br>\n<br>\nConform\u00e9ment au principe selon lequel chaque \u00eatre humain a un \u00e9gal droit \u00e0 polluer, les revenus g\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9s par la vente de permis pourraient financer un revenu de base mondial. <strong>Chaque adulte recevrait 20\u20ac par mois<\/strong>, sortant ainsi de l'extr\u00eame pauvret\u00e9 600 millions de personnes qui gagnent moins de 2$ par jour.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Le <span class=\"national\">Fran\u00e7ais<\/span> moyen perdrait financi\u00e8rement 15\u20ac par mois<\/strong>&nbsp;(car il ferait face \u00e0 environ <span id=\"price_increase\">1<\/span>% de hausses de prix, ce qui est sup\u00e9rieur aux 20\u20ac par mois&nbsp;qu'il recevrait).<br>\n<br>\nLa mesure serait mise en place d\u00e8s que 100 pays s'accordent dessus. Les pays qui refuseraient de participer \u00e0 la mesure pourraient faire face \u00e0 des sanctions (comme des droits de douane) du reste du monde et seraient exclus du revenu de base.<br>\n<br>\n<br><b>\nSoutenez-vous le Plan mondial pour le climat ?<\/b>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\t\n\t\/\/ Loads CSV and create variables from the column corresponding to Q_Language\n\t$j(document).ready(function($j){\t\n\t\t$j.ajax({\n\t\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\/\/ Iterate through the rows and create variables dynamically\n\t\t\tfor (let i = 1; i < rows.length-1; i++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst name = rows[i][0]; \/\/ Assuming the row name is in the first column\n\t\t\t\tconst value = rows[i][col];\n\t\t\t\twindow[name] = value; \n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\t$j(\".\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`Variable ${name} created with value: ${value}`);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t\t});\n\t});\n});","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gcs_support_no_info","QuestionID":"QID5","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Ci-dessous, nous d\u00e9crivons une mesure politique, sur laquelle nous allons sonder votre opinion. P...","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Oui"},"5":{"Display":"Non"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Oui"},"5":{"Display":"Non"}}}},"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div>Do you support the following policy?<br>\nTo ensure that you have attentively read the description,&nbsp;<strong>we will ask some comprehension questions later in the survey: those who get correct answers can win <span id=\"amount_lottery\">[amount_lottery: $100]<\/span><\/strong>.<\/div>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Global Climate Scheme:<\/strong><\/u>&nbsp;<br><br>\nIn 2015, all countries agreed to contain global warming \"well below +2&nbsp;\u00b0C\". To achieve this,&nbsp;<strong>there is a maximum amount of greenhouse gases we can emit globally<\/strong>.&nbsp;<br><br>\nTo meet the climate target, a limited number of permits to emit greenhouse gases would be issued globally. Polluting firms would be required to buy permits to cover their greenhouse gas emissions. Such a policy would&nbsp;<strong>make fossil fuel companies pay<\/strong>&nbsp;for their emissions and gradually raise the price of fossil fuels.&nbsp;<strong>Higher prices would encourage people and companies to use less fossil fuels, reducing greenhouse gas emissions.<br><\/strong><br>\nIn accordance with the principle that each human has an equal right to pollute, the revenues generated by the sale of permits could finance a global basic income.&nbsp;<strong>Every adult would receive <span class=\"amount_bi\">[amount_bi: $20]<\/span><span class=\"periodicity\">[periodicity: per month]<\/span><\/strong>, thereby lifting 600 million people who earn less than $2 a day out of extreme poverty.<br>\n<strong>The typical <span class=\"national\">[national: American]<\/span> would lose out financially <span id=\"amount_lost\">[amount_lost: $105]<\/span><span class=\"periodicity\">[periodicity: per month]<\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;(as he or she would face around <span id=\"price_increase\">[price_increase: 2]<\/span>% in price increases, which is higher than the <span class=\"amount_bi\">[amount_bi: $20]<\/span><span class=\"periodicity\">[periodicity: per month]<\/span> they would receive).<br><br>\nThe policy could be implemented as soon as 100 countries agree to it. Countries that would refuse to take part in the policy could face sanctions (like tariffs) from the rest of the world and would be excluded from the basic income program.<br><br>\n<br><b>\nDo you support the Global Climate Scheme?\n<\/b><div><\/div>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID50","SecondaryAttribute":"Imagine a wealth tax applying on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all count..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Answers":{"1":{"Display":0},"2":{"Display":10},"3":{"Display":20},"4":{"Display":30},"5":{"Display":40},"6":{"Display":50},"7":{"Display":60},"8":{"Display":70},"9":{"Display":80},"10":{"Display":90},"11":{"Display":100}},"ChoiceOrder":["1"],"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Percent of wealth tax that should go to low-income countries"}},"Configuration":{"CSSliderMax":100,"CSSliderMin":0,"CustomStart":false,"GridLines":10,"MobileFirst":true,"NotApplicable":false,"NumDecimals":"0","QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","ShowValue":true,"SnapToGrid":true},"DataExportTag":"tax_global_share","DataVisibility":{"Hidden":false,"Private":false},"DefaultChoices":false,"GradingData":[],"Labels":[],"Language":{"DE":{"QuestionText":"<div>Stellen Sie sich eine Verm\u00f6genssteuer vor, die f\u00fcr Haushalte mit einem Nettoverm\u00f6gen von \u00fcber 5 Millionen \u20ac gilt und in allen L\u00e4ndern der Welt erlassen wird.<\/div>\n\n<div>In Deutschland w\u00fcrden die eingenommenen Steuereinnahmen 44 Milliarden \u20ac pro Jahr betragen (d. h. 1,3 % des deutschen Bruttoinlandsprodukts), w\u00e4hrend es in allen L\u00e4ndern mit niedrigem Einkommen zusammen 1 Milliarde Euro betragen w\u00fcrde (700 Millionen Menschen leben in einem\u00a0der 28 L\u00e4nder mit niedrigem Einkommen, die meisten davon in Afrika).<\/div>\n\n<div>Jedes Land w\u00fcrde einen Teil der Einnahmen behalten, die es einnimmt, und der verbleibende Teil w\u00fcrde auf globaler Ebene geb\u00fcndelt, um Infrastruktur und \u00f6ffentliche Dienstleistungen in L\u00e4ndern mit niedrigem Einkommen zu finanzieren.<\/div>\n\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n\n<div>Welcher Prozentsatz sollte zur\u00a0finanziellen Unterst\u00fctzung von einkommensschwachen L\u00e4ndern herangezogen werden (statt im Staatshaushalt des Landes zur\u00fcckbehalten zu werden)?<\/div>\n","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Prozent der weltweiten Verm\u00f6genssteuer, die an einkommensschwache L\u00e4nder gehen soll"}},"Labels":[]},"EN-GB":{"QuestionText":"<div>Imagine a wealth tax on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all countries around the world.<\/div>\n\n<div>In the UK, the tax revenues collected would amount to \u00a320 billion per year (that is, 0.9% of\u00a0UK GDP), while it would amount to $1 billion in all low-income countries taken together (28 countries, home to 700 million people, most of them in Africa).<\/div>\n\n<div>Each country would retain part of the revenues it collects, and the remaining part would be pooled at the global level to finance infrastructure and public services in low-income countries.<\/div>\n\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n\n<div>What percentage should be pooled to finance low-income countries (instead of retained in the country's national budget)?<\/div>\n","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Percent of global wealth tax that should go to low-income countries"}},"Labels":[]},"ES-ES":{"QuestionText":"Imagine un impuesto sobre el patrimonio que se aplique a los hogares con un patrimonio neto superior a 5 millones de euros, promulgado en todos los pa\u00edses del mundo.<br \/>\nEn Espa\u00f1a, los ingresos fiscales recaudados ser\u00edan de 5 mil millones de euros por a\u00f1o (es decir, el 0.4% del PIB de Espa\u00f1a), mientras que ser\u00edan 1 mil millones de euros en todos los pa\u00edses de bajos ingresos en su conjunto (28 pa\u00edses, la mayor\u00eda de ellos en \u00c1frica, donde viven 700 millones de personas).<br \/>\nCada pa\u00eds retendr\u00eda parte de los ingresos que recauda y la parte restante se mancomunar\u00eda a nivel mundial para financiar infraestructura y servicios p\u00fablicos en pa\u00edses de bajos ingresos.<br \/>\n\u00a0<br \/>\n\u00bfQu\u00e9 porcentaje debe agruparse para financiar a los pa\u00edses de bajos ingresos (en lugar de retenerse en el presupuesto nacional del pa\u00eds)","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Porcentaje del impuesto mundial sobre el patrimonio que deber\u00eda ir a pa\u00edses de bajos ingresos"}},"Labels":[]},"FR":{"QuestionText":"<div>Imaginez un imp\u00f4t sur la fortune appliqu\u00e9 aux m\u00e9nages dont le patrimoine est sup\u00e9rieur \u00e0 5 millions d'euros, mis en \u0153uvre dans tous les pays du monde.<\/div>\n\n<div>En France, les recettes de la taxe seraient de 16 milliards d'euros par an (soit 0,7\u00a0% du PIB fran\u00e7ais), alors qu'elles seraient de 1\u00a0milliard d'euros dans l'ensemble des pays \u00e0 faibles revenus (soit 28 pays, o\u00f9 vivent 700\u00a0millions de personnes, pour la plupart en Afrique).<\/div>\n\n<div>Chaque pays conserverait une partie des revenus qu'il per\u00e7oit, et le reste serait mis en commun au niveau mondial pour financer des infrastructures et des services publics dans les pays \u00e0 faibles revenus.<\/div>\n\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n\n<div>Quel pourcentage devrait \u00eatre mis en commun pour financer les pays \u00e0 faibles revenus (au lieu d'\u00eatre retenu dans le budget national du pays)\u00a0?<\/div>\n","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Pourcentage de l'imp\u00f4t sur la fortune mondial qui devrait aller aux pays \u00e0 faibles revenus"}},"Labels":[]}},"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":4,"QuestionDescription":"Imagine a wealth tax applying on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all count...","QuestionID":"QID50","QuestionText":"<div>Imagine a wealth tax applying on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all countries around the world.<\/div>\n\n<div>In the UK, the tax revenues collected would be \u00a320 billion per year (that is, 0.7% of&nbsp;UK GDP), while it would be $1 billion in all low-income countries taken together (700 million people live in a low-income country, most of them in Africa).<\/div>\n\n<div>Each country would retain part of the revenues it collects, and the remaining part would be pooled at the global level to finance infrastructure and public services in low-income countries.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>What percentage should be pooled to finance low-income countries (instead of retained in the country's national budget)?<\/div>","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div>Imagine a wealth tax applying on households with net worth above \u00a35 million, enacted in all countries around the world.<\/div>\n\n<div>In the UK, the tax revenues collected would be \u00a320 billion per year (that is, 0.7% of&nbsp;UK GDP), while it would be $1 billion in all low-income countries taken together (700 million people live in a low-income country, most of them in Africa).<\/div>\n\n<div>Each country would retain part of the revenues it collects, and the remaining part would be pooled at the global level to finance infrastructure and public services in low-income countries.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>What percentage should be pooled to finance low-income countries (instead of retained in the country's national budget)?<\/div>","QuestionType":"Slider","Selector":"HSLIDER","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">variant_substitute<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 0 <\/span>","LeftOperand":"variant_substitute","LogicType":"EmbeddedField","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"0","Type":"Expression"},"1":{"Conjuction":"And","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">And<\/spa