xn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID9","SecondaryAttribute":"Below is a map showing a possible set of countries that would participate in the Global Climate S...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Below is a map showing a possible set of countries that would participate in the Global Climate Scheme previously described.<br>\n<br>\nThese countries include China, India, as well as all Africa, Latin America, South-Asia and South-East Asia.<br>\nCollectively, these 119 countries account for 56% of global emissions<span id=\"text_emissions_with\"> (if <span id=\"ics_country\">[ics_country: the U.S.]<\/span> joined them, <span id=\"emissions_mid_with\">[emissions_mid_with: 70]<\/span>% of global emissions would be covered)<\/span>.<br>\n<br>\n<img width=\"100\" style=\"width: 100%\" src=\"https:\/\/github.com\/bixiou\/robustness_global_redistr\/raw\/main\/figures\/maps_participation\/GCS_mid.png\" id=\"gcs_mid\">","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gcs_mid","QuestionID":"QID9","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Below is a map showing a possible set of countries that would participate in the Global Climate S...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Vous trouverez ci-dessous une carte montrant un ensemble possible de pays qui participeraient au Plan mondial pour le climat d\u00e9crit pr\u00e9c\u00e9demment.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nCes pays comprennent la Chine, l\u2019Inde, ainsi que toute l\u2019Afrique, l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine, l\u2019Asie du Sud et l\u2019Asie du Sud-Est.<br \/>\nEnsemble, ces 119 pays totalisent 56\u00a0% des \u00e9missions mondiales<span id=\"text_emissions_with\"> (si <span class=\"ics_country\">les \u00c9tats-Unis<\/span> les rejoignait, <span id=\"emissions_mid_with\">70<\/span>\u00a0% des \u00e9missions mondiales seraient couvertes)<\/span>.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<img id=\"gcs_mid\" src=\"https:\/\/github.com\/bixiou\/robustness_global_redistr\/raw\/main\/figures\/maps_participation\/GCS_mid.png\" style=\"width: 100%\" width=\"100\" \/>"}},"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Below is a map showing a possible set of countries that would participate in the Global Climate Scheme previously described.<br>\n<br>\nThese countries include China, India, as well as all Africa, Latin America, South-Asia and South-East Asia.<br>\nCollectively, these 119 countries account for 56% of global emissions<span id=\"text_emissions_with\"> (if <span id=\"ics_country\">[ics_country: the U.S.]<\/span> joined them, <span id=\"emissions_mid_with\">[emissions_mid_with: 70]<\/span>% of global emissions would be covered)<\/span>.<br>\n<br>\n<img width=\"100\" style=\"width: 100%\" src=\"https:\/\/github.com\/bixiou\/robustness_global_redistr\/raw\/main\/figures\/maps_participation\/GCS_mid.png\" id=\"gcs_mid\">","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_gcs\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tconst time_before = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"time_warm_glow_substitute\");\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"duration_gcs\", Date.now()\/1000 - time_before);\n\t\n\t\/\/ Loads CSV and create variables from the column corresponding to Q_Language\n\t$j(document).ready(function($j){\t\n\t\t$j.ajax({\n\t\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\t\t\tconst country = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"country\");  \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tif (country == \"CH\") { $j(\"#text_emissions_with\").html(\"\"); }\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t$j(\"#gcs_mid\").attr(\"src\", \"https:\/\/github.com\/bixiou\/robustness_global_redistr\/raw\/main\/figures\/maps_participation\/GCS_mid_\" + language + \".png\");\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\/\/ Iterate through the rows and create variables dynamically\n\t\t\tfor (let i = 1; i < rows.length-1; i++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst name = rows[i][0]; \/\/ Assuming the row name is in the first column\n\t\t\t\tconst value = rows[i][col];\n\t\t\t\twindow[name] = value; \n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\t$j(\".\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`Variable ${name} created with value: ${value}`);\n\t\t\t}\t\t\n\n\t\t\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"variant_gcs\", \"mid\"); \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t\t});\n\t});\n});"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID90","SecondaryAttribute":"[text_vote: Which candidate did you vote for in the [election: 2024 European Parliament election]...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<span id=\"text_vote\">[text_vote: Which candidate did you vote for in the <span class=\"election\">[election: 2024 European Parliament election]<\/span>?<br>Even if you did not vote in the <span class=\"election\">[election: 2024 European Parliament election]<\/span>, please indicate the candidate that you were most likely to have voted for or who represents your views more closely.]<\/span>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function()\n{\n\tconst voted = '${q:\/\/QID44\/SelectedChoicesRecode}';\n\n\t$j.ajax({\n\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rowNames = rows.slice(1).map(row => row[0]); \n\t\t\tconst values = rows.slice(1).map(row => row[col]);\n\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tif (voted == 1 || voted == \"Yes\" || voted == \"\u306f\u3044\" || voted == \"Oui\" || voted == \"Ja\" || voted == \"Si\" || voted == \"\u0414\u0430\" || voted == \"S\u00ec\" || voted == \"S\u00ed\" || voted == \"Tak\" || voted == \"\u0646\u0639\u0645\" || voted == \"\u305d\u3046\u3060\") {\n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#text_vote\").html(values[rowNames.indexOf(\"text_vote_voted\")]);\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#text_vote\").html(values[rowNames.indexOf(\"text_vote_didnt_vote\")]);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t$j(\"#election\").html(election);\n\t\t\t$j(\".election\").html(election);\n\n\t\t},\n\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t});\n\n});","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"vote_PL","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SACOL","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","NumColumns":2},"QuestionDescription":"[text_vote: Which candidate did you vote for in the [election: 2024 European Parliament election]...","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"United Right (Law and Justice, Sovereign Poland...)"},"5":{"Display":"Civic Coalition (Civic Platform, Polish Initiative...)"},"6":{"Display":"Polish People's Party"},"13":{"Display":"Prefer not to say"},"15":{"Display":"The Left (New Left...)"},"18":{"Display":"Other"},"19":{"Display":"Confederation (New Hope, National Movement, Confederation of the Polish Crown...)"},"22":{"Display":"Poland 2050"}},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">country<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> PL <\/span>","LeftOperand":"country","LogicType":"EmbeddedField","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"PL","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":false},"ChoiceOrder":["5","4","19","6","22","15","18","13"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Pour quel candidat avez-vous vot\u00e9 lors des \u00e9lections g\u00e9n\u00e9rales britanniques de 2019\u00a0?","Choices":{"5":{"Display":"Travail"},"4":{"Display":"Conservateur"},"19":{"Display":"F\u00eate du Brexit"},"6":{"Display":"D\u00e9mocrates lib\u00e9raux"},"22":{"Display":"Pologne 2050"},"15":{"Display":"Vert"},"18":{"Display":"Autre"},"13":{"Display":"Je pr\u00e9f\u00e8re ne pas le dire"}}}},"NextChoiceId":23,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID90","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<span id=\"text_vote\">[text_vote: Which candidate did you vote for in the <span class=\"election\">[election: 2024 European Parliament election]<\/span>?<br>Even if you did not vote in the <span class=\"election\">[election: 2024 European Parliament election]<\/span>, please indicate the candidate that you were most likely to have voted for or who represents your views more closely.]<\/span>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID91","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"Q91","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 1"},"2":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 2"},"3":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 3"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID91"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID92","SecondaryAttribute":"What according to you is the greatest injustice of all?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"What according to you is the greatest injustice of all?<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"injustice_field","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ESTB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"What according to you is the greatest injustice of all?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Selon vous, quelle est la plus grande injustice qui soit ?"}},"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionID":"QID92","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_socios_demos\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_field\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tconst time_before = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"time_consent\");\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"duration_socios_demos\", Date.now()\/1000 - time_before);\n\t\n});\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is fully displayed*\/\n\n});\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnUnload(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is unloaded*\/\n\n});","QuestionText_Unsafe":"What according to you is the greatest injustice of all?<br>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID93","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q93","QuestionID":"QID93","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":0},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":[]},"NextChoiceId":32,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Timing"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID94","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q94","QuestionID":"QID94","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","MinSeconds":"0","MaxSeconds":"0"},"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"Validation":"None","GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":[]},"NextChoiceId":16,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Timing"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID95","SecondaryAttribute":"At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of \"climate...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of \"climate finance\": the financing of climate action from developed countries in developing countries.<\/b> <span id=\"developed_note\">[developed_note: (Note that we consider Saudi Arabia to be a developed country in this question.)]<\/span><br><br><b>There are two kinds of climate finance: grants (that is, donations) and loans. In 2022, $26 billion was provided as grants and the rest as loans, for a total of $116 billion.&nbsp;<\/b><br><br>In 2009, developed countries agreed to mobilize $100 billion per year in climate finance by 2020. In 2024, they committed to raise this goal to $300 billion by 2035. None of the goals specify which share should be provided as grants.<br><br>Below are different positions on the amount of climate finance that should be provided in 2035, all expressed in grant-equivalent terms (that is, not counting loans):<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; $0: There should be no contributions from developed countries to climate action in developing countries.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; $26 billion (0.04% of developed countries' GDP): The current amount, consistent with the old (2020) goal.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $100 billion (0.14% of GDP): The old (2020) goal, if all climate finance were provided as grants.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $300 billion (0.43% of GDP): The new (2035) goal, if all climate finance were provided as grants.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $600 billion (0.86% of GDP):&nbsp;The goal called for by India, a position shared by most developing countries.<br>- $1,000 billion (1.43% of GDP): The goal called for by Climate Action Network (a network of NGOs including Greenpeace, Oxfam, and WWF).<br>- $5,000 billion (7.14% of GDP): The goal called for by Demand Climate Justice (a network of NGOs including 350.org and&nbsp;the World Council of Churches)<br><br><b>If you could choose the amount of climate finance provided by developed countries to developing countries in 2035, what amount would you choose (in grant-equivalent terms)?<\/b><br>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_warm_glow_realism\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tconst time_before = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"time_ics\");\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"duration_warm_glow_realism\", Date.now()\/1000 - time_before);\n\t\n\t\/\/ Loads CSV and create variables from the column corresponding to Q_Language\n\t$j(document).ready(function($j){\t\n\t\t$j.ajax({\n\t\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\/\/ Iterate through the rows and create variables dynamically\n\t\t\tfor (let i = 1; i < rows.length-1; i++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst name = rows[i][0]; \/\/ Assuming the row name is in the first column\n\t\t\t\tconst value = rows[i][col];\n\t\t\t\twindow[name] = value; \n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`Variable ${name} created with value: ${value}`);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t\t});\n\t});\n});","DataExportTag":"ncqg_full","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of \"climate...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"$0"},"2":{"Display":"$300 billion"},"3":{"Display":"$600 billion"},"4":{"Display":"$26 billion"},"5":{"Display":"$100 billion"},"6":{"Display":"$1,000 billion"},"7":{"Display":"$5,000 billion"}},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">variant_ncqg_maritime<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 2 <\/span>","LeftOperand":"variant_ncqg_maritime","LogicType":"EmbeddedField","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"2","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":false},"ChoiceOrder":["1","4","5","2","3","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Lors des n\u00e9gociations internationales sur le climat, les pays en d\u00e9veloppement appellent \u00e0 davantage de \u00ab finance climat \u00bb : le financement de l\u2019action climatique par les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s dans les pays en d\u00e9veloppement. <span id=\"developed_note\">[developed_note\u00a0: (Notez que nous consid\u00e9rons l\u2019Arabie saoudite comme un pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9 dans cette question.)]<\/span><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<b>Il existe deux types de finance climat : les subventions (c\u2019est-\u00e0-dire les dons) et les pr\u00eats. En 2022, 26 milliards de dollars ont \u00e9t\u00e9 accord\u00e9s sous forme de subventions et le reste sous forme de pr\u00eats, pour un total de 116 milliards de dollars.<\/b><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<b>En 2009, les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s ont convenu de mobiliser 100 milliards de dollars par an en finance climat d\u2019ici 2020. En 2024, ils se sont engag\u00e9s \u00e0 porter cet objectif \u00e0 300 milliards de dollars d\u2019ici 2035. Aucun de ces objectifs ne pr\u00e9cise quelle part devrait \u00eatre vers\u00e9e sous forme de subventions.<\/b><br \/>\n<br \/>\nVous trouverez ci-dessous diff\u00e9rentes positions sur le montant de finance climat qui devrait \u00eatre fourni en 2035, toutes exprim\u00e9es en termes d'\u00e9quivalent-subvention (c'est-\u00e0-dire sans compter les pr\u00eats) :<br \/>\n- 0\u00a0: Les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s ne devraient pas contribuer \u00e0 l\u2019action climatique dans les pays en d\u00e9veloppement.<br \/>\n- 26 milliards de dollars (0,04 % du PIB des pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s) : le montant actuel, coh\u00e9rent avec l\u2019ancien objectif (pour 2020).<br \/>\n- 100 milliards de dollars (0,14 % du PIB) : l\u2019ancien objectif (pour 2020), si\u00a0toute la finance climat \u00e9tait fournie sous forme de subventions.<br \/>\n- 300 milliards de dollars (0,43 % du PIB) : le nouvel objectif (pour 2035), si toute la finance climat \u00e9tait fournie sous forme de subventions.<br \/>\n- 600 milliards de dollars (0,86 % du PIB) : l\u2019objectif d\u00e9fendu par l\u2019Inde, une position partag\u00e9e par la plupart des pays en d\u00e9veloppement.<br \/>\n- 1 000 milliards de dollars (1,43 % du PIB) : l\u2019objectif d\u00e9fendu par le Climate Action Network (un r\u00e9seau d\u2019ONG comprenant Greenpeace, Oxfam et WWF).<br \/>\n- 5 000 milliards de dollars (7,14 % du PIB) : l'objectif d\u00e9fendu par Demand Climate Justice (un r\u00e9seau d'ONG comprenant 350.org et le Conseil \u0153cum\u00e9nique des \u00c9glises)<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<b>Si vous pouviez choisir le montant de la finance climat fournie par les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s aux pays en d\u00e9veloppement en 2035, quel montant choisiriez-vous (en termes d\u2019\u00e9quivalent-subvention) ?<\/b>","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"0\u00a0$"},"2":{"Display":"300 milliards de dollars"},"3":{"Display":"600 milliards de dollars"},"4":{"Display":"26 milliards de dollars"},"5":{"Display":"100 milliards de dollars"},"6":{"Display":"1 000 milliards de dollars"},"7":{"Display":"5 000 milliards de dollars"}}}},"NextChoiceId":8,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID95","Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"ConsistentScaleReversal":false,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"None"},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<b>At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of \"climate finance\": the financing of climate action from developed countries in developing countries.<\/b> <span id=\"developed_note\">[developed_note: (Note that we consider Saudi Arabia to be a developed country in this question.)]<\/span><br><br><b>There are two kinds of climate finance: grants (that is, donations) and loans. In 2022, $26 billion was provided as grants and the rest as loans, for a total of $116 billion.&nbsp;<\/b><br><br>In 2009, developed countries agreed to mobilize $100 billion per year in climate finance by 2020. In 2024, they committed to raise this goal to $300 billion by 2035. None of the goals specify which share should be provided as grants.<br><br>Below are different positions on the amount of climate finance that should be provided in 2035, all expressed in grant-equivalent terms (that is, not counting loans):<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; $0: There should be no contributions from developed countries to climate action in developing countries.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; $26 billion (0.04% of developed countries' GDP): The current amount, consistent with the old (2020) goal.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $100 billion (0.14% of GDP): The old (2020) goal, if all climate finance were provided as grants.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $300 billion (0.43% of GDP): The new (2035) goal, if all climate finance were provided as grants.<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; $600 billion (0.86% of GDP):&nbsp;The goal called for by India, a position shared by most developing countries.<br>- $1,000 billion (1.43% of GDP): The goal called for by Climate Action Network (a network of NGOs including Greenpeace, Oxfam, and WWF).<br>- $5,000 billion (7.14% of GDP): The goal called for by Demand Climate Justice (a network of NGOs including 350.org and&nbsp;the World Council of Churches)<br><br><b>If you could choose the amount of climate finance provided by developed countries to developing countries in 2035, what amount would you choose (in grant-equivalent terms)?<\/b><br>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID96","SecondaryAttribute":"What do you need or wish?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"What do you need or wish?","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"wish_field","QuestionID":"QID96","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ML","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","InputWidth":680,"InputHeight":114},"QuestionDescription":"What do you need or wish?","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"PL":[]},"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID97","SecondaryAttribute":"\"Climate finance\" designates the financing of climate action from developed countries in developi...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>\"Climate finance\" designates the financing of climate action from developed countries in developing countries.<\/b> <span id=\"developed_note\">[developed_note: (Note that we consider Saudi Arabia to be a developed country in this question.)]<\/span><br><br><b>There are two kinds of climate finance: grants (that is, donations) and loans. The large majority is currently provided as loans.&nbsp;<\/b><br><br>In 2009, developed countries agreed to mobilize $100 billion per year in climate finance. In 2024, they committed to triple this goal by 2035. None of the goals specify which share should be provided as grants.&nbsp;<br>At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of climate finance, particularly in the form of grants.<br><br><b>If you could choose the level of climate finance provided by developed countries to developing countries in 2035, what would you choose?<\/b><br>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"time_warm_glow_realism\", Date.now()\/1000);\n\tconst time_before = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"time_ics\");\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(\"duration_warm_glow_realism\", Date.now()\/1000 - time_before);\n\t\n\t\/\/ Loads CSV and create variables from the column corresponding to Q_Language\n\t$j(document).ready(function($j){\t\n\t\t$j.ajax({\n\t\t\turl:\"https:\/\/wumarketing.eu.qualtrics.com\/ControlPanel\/File.php?F=F_yuKEs6pwxsAid44\",\n\t\t\tsuccess: function(csv){\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst language = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"Q_Language\"); \n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\tconst rows = csv.split('\\n').map(row => row.split('|'));\n\t\t\tconst headers = rows[0];\n\t\t\tconst col = headers.indexOf(language);\n\n\t\t\tif (col === -1) {\n\t\t\t\tconsole.error(\"Column 'language' not found in the CSV file.\");\n\t\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\/\/ Iterate through the rows and create variables dynamically\n\t\t\tfor (let i = 1; i < rows.length-1; i++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst name = rows[i][0]; \/\/ Assuming the row name is in the first column\n\t\t\t\tconst value = rows[i][col];\n\t\t\t\twindow[name] = value; \n\t\t\t\t$j(\"#\" + name).html(value);\n\t\t\t\tconsole.log(`Variable ${name} created with value: ${value}`);\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\terror: function(){ alert('Data could not be loaded');}\n\t\t});\n\t});\n});","DataExportTag":"ncqg","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"\"Climate finance\" designates the financing of climate action from developed countries in developi...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"<strong>Stop <\/strong>all provision of climate finance."},"2":{"Display":"<strong>Meet the newly agreed goal<\/strong> by tripling grants and loans ($100 billion in grants, or 0.15% of GDP)."},"3":{"Display":"<strong>Increase climate finance to a level between what developed countries have agreed and what developing countries are asking for<\/strong> ($300 billion in grants, or 0.45% of GDP)."},"4":{"Display":"<strong>Reduce <\/strong>the provision of climate finance."},"5":{"Display":"<strong>Maintain current contributions<\/strong> ($26 billion per year in grants, that is 0.04% of developed countries&#39; GDP, and $80 billion in loans, or 0.1% of GDP)."},"6":{"Display":"<strong>Increase climate finance to match what developing countries are asking for <\/strong>($600 billion in grants, or 0.9% of GDP)."},"7":{"Display":"<strong>Increase climate finance to match what NGOs are asking for<\/strong> (at least $1,000 billion per year in grants, that is 1.4% of GDP, is what Greenpeace, Oxfam, WWF, and the World Council of Churches ask for)."}},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">variant_ncqg_maritime<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 1 <\/span>","LeftOperand":"variant_ncqg_maritime","LogicType":"EmbeddedField","Operator":"EqualTo","RightOperand":"1","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression","inPage":false},"ChoiceOrder":["1","4","5","2","3","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"<strong>La \u00ab finance climat \u00bb d\u00e9signe le financement de l\u2019action climatique dans les pays en d\u00e9veloppement par les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s.\u00a0<\/strong><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<b>Il existe deux types de finance climat : les subventions (c\u2019est-\u00e0-dire les dons) et les pr\u00eats. La grande majorit\u00e9 est actuellement fournie sous forme de pr\u00eats.<\/b><br \/>\n<br \/>\nEn 2009, les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s ont convenu de mobiliser 100 milliards de dollars par an en finance climat. En 2024, ils se sont engag\u00e9s \u00e0 tripler cet objectif d\u2019ici 2035. Aucun des objectifs ne pr\u00e9cise quelle part devrait \u00eatre vers\u00e9e sous forme de subventions.<br \/>\nLors des n\u00e9gociations internationales sur le climat, les pays en d\u00e9veloppement r\u00e9clament davantage de finance climat, notamment sous forme de subventions.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<b>Si vous pouviez choisir le niveau de finance climat fourni par les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s aux pays en d\u00e9veloppement en 2035, que choisiriez-vous ?<\/b>","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"<strong>Arr\u00eater <\/strong>toute contribution \u00e0 la finance climat."},"4":{"Display":"<strong>R\u00e9duire <\/strong>les contributions \u00e0 la finance climat."},"5":{"Display":"<strong>Maintenir les contributions actuelles<\/strong> (26 milliards de dollars de subventions, soit 0,04 % du PIB des pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s, et 80 milliards de dollars de pr\u00eats, soit 0,1 % du PIB)."},"2":{"Display":"<strong>Atteindre le nouvel objectif fix\u00e9 <\/strong>en triplant les subventions et les pr\u00eats (100 milliards de dollars de subventions, soit 0,15\u00a0% du PIB)."},"3":{"Display":"<strong>Augmenter la finance climat \u00e0 un niveau compris entre ce que les pays d\u00e9velopp\u00e9s ont accept\u00e9 et ce que les pays en d\u00e9veloppement demandent<\/strong>\u00a0(300 milliards de dollars de subventions, soit 0,45\u00a0% du PIB)."},"6":{"Display":"<strong>Augmenter la finance climat \u00e0 hauteur des demandes des pays en d\u00e9veloppement<\/strong> (600 milliards de dollars par an en subventions, soit 0,9 % du PIB)."},"7":{"Display":"<strong>Augmenter la finance climat \u00e0 hauteur de ce que demandent les ONG<\/strong> (au moins 1 000 milliards de dollars de subventions, soit 1,4\u00a0% du PIB, comme demand\u00e9 par Greenpeace, Oxfam, le WWF et le Conseil \u0153cum\u00e9nique des \u00c9glises)."}}}},"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID97","Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"ConsistentScaleReversal":false,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"ScaleReversal"},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<b>\"Climate finance\" designates the financing of climate action from developed countries in developing countries.<\/b> <span id=\"developed_note\">[developed_note: (Note that we consider Saudi Arabia to be a developed country in this question.)]<\/span><br><br><b>There are two kinds of climate finance: grants (that is, donations) and loans. The large majority is currently provided as loans.&nbsp;<\/b><br><br>In 2009, developed countries agreed to mobilize $100 billion per year in climate finance. In 2024, they committed to triple this goal by 2035. None of the goals specify which share should be provided as grants.&nbsp;<br>At international climate negotiations, developing countries call for larger provision of climate finance, particularly in the form of grants.<br><br><b>If you could choose the level of climate finance provided by developed countries to developing countries in 2035, what would you choose?<\/b><br>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID98","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DataExportTag":"zipcode","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 1"},"2":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 2"},"3":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 3"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID98"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID99","SecondaryAttribute":"Quel est votre code postal ? Nous demandons le code postal afin d'\u00e9quilibrer l'\u00e9chantillon en ter.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Quel est votre code postal ?<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Nous demandons le code postal afin d&#39;&eacute;quilibrer l&#39;&eacute;chantillon en termes de type d&#39;urbanisation (urbain ou rural). L&#39;enqu&ecirc;te sera stopp&eacute;e si votre code postal n&#39;est pas reconnu.<\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"zipcode","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"SL","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","InputWidth":244,"InputHeight":29},"QuestionDescription":"Quel est votre code postal ? Nous demandons le code postal afin d'\u00e9quilibrer l'\u00e9chantillon en ter...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","ForceResponseType":"RequestResponse","Type":"CustomValidation","MinChars":"1","ValidDateType":"DateWithFormat","ValidPhoneType":"ValidUSPhone","ValidZipType":"ValidUSZip","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"QuestionID":"QID99","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID99\/ChoiceTextEntryValue","Operator":"MatchesRegex","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID99","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID99\/ChoiceTextEntryValue","RightOperand":"^[0-9]{5}$","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Quel est votre code postal ? Nous demandons le code postal afin d'\u00e9quilibrer l'\u00e9chantillon en ter...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Text Response<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Matches Regex<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> ^[0-9]{5}$ <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"messageID":"MS_Mlvv9hBU0UM4MSJ","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0","libraryID":"UR_9ohR5yK9iaG0JTg","description":"Require valid zipcode"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":{"FR":{"QuestionText":"Quel est votre code postal ?<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Nous demandons le code postal afin d'\u00e9quilibrer l'\u00e9chantillon en termes de type d'urbanisation (urbain ou rural). L'enqu\u00eate sera stopp\u00e9e si votre code postal n'est pas reconnu.<\/span>"}},"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionID":"QID99","QuestionText_Unsafe":"What is your zipcode?<br>\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">We ask for the zipcode to balance the sample in terms of degree of urbanization (rural, town or city). The survey will be terminated if your zipcode is not recognized.<\/span>"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_abLGdxn76dMdkCq","Element":"STAT","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Statistics","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"MobileCompatible":true,"ID":"Survey Statistics"}}]}